      "ExportWorkoutModal.jsx: fixed the reported flickering/glitching during \"Save image\" generation, confirmed to happen specifically during html2canvas's capture (not on open or while toggling) and to self-resolve after roughly 10 seconds. The scroll-position fix shipped earlier this version (see below) was real but not the culprit here -- the actual cause was the progress-photo Story background: it's a Supabase signed URL, loaded cross-origin via crossOrigin=\"anonymous\" so html2canvas's capture doesn't taint the canvas, and when that live cross-origin fetch stalled (flaky network, CORS quirk on the signed URL), html2canvas sat waiting on its imageTimeout before giving up -- the ~10s hang. Fix: pre-fetch the photo and convert it to a same-origin data URL as soon as the modal opens (well before Save Image is tapped), and use that for the `<img>` background instead of the live remote URL. The capture then never needs a network fetch at all, so there's nothing left to hang on. Falls back to the original remote-URL + crossOrigin path if the conversion fails, now with imageTimeout capped at 3000ms instead of html2canvas's ~15s default so that fallback path can't stall nearly as long either.",
